CAT = "nzreLicensing"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
("Who may carry out real estate agency work in New Zealand?",
 "A licensee or an exempt person", ["Anyone holding a sales certificate", "Any adult who has a client", "A company director only"],
 "Section 6 of the Real Estate Agents Act 2008 says a person must not do agency work unless licensed (and acting within that licence) or exempt under sections 7 to 9 or another enactment."),
("A lawyer sells a client's land as part of their legal work. Can the lawyer also charge a commission?",
 "No, only professional fees", ["Yes, if the client agrees", "Yes, on top of their fees", "Yes, but only on houses"],
 "Lawyers and conveyancers are exempt from licensing, but for the sale of land or a business they cannot be paid commission in addition to, or instead of, their professional charges (section 7)."),
("Who may sell land by auction without holding a real estate licence?",
 "A registered auctioneer", ["A branch manager only", "Any lawyer's assistant", "A holder of a property degree"],
 "A person registered as an auctioneer under the Auctioneers Act 2013 may sell or offer to sell land by auction (section 8)."),
("What is the minimum age to be licensed as a salesperson?",
 "18 years", ["16 years", "20 years", "21 years"],
 "An individual must be at least 18, not prohibited, fit and proper, and hold the prescribed qualification to be licensed as a salesperson (section 36)."),
("Which requirement applies to an agent or branch manager licence but not to a salesperson licence?",
 "Three years of experience", ["A fit and proper assessment", "A minimum age of 18 years", "The prescribed qualification"],
 "Section 36 asks agents and branch managers for three years of agency work in the last ten years. A salesperson needs age, fitness, no prohibition and the qualification."),
("What does the Act require of how a salesperson is managed?",
 "Proper supervision by a manager", ["Quarterly review by the Registrar", "Direction from each vendor", "Supervision in the first year only"],
 "Section 50 requires a salesperson to be properly supervised and managed by an agent or branch manager, with enough direction and control to ensure competent, compliant work."),
("An agent engages a salesperson as an independent contractor. For the contractor's mistakes, the agent is:",
 "Liable as if an employer", ["Not liable at all", "Liable only for fraud", "Liable only to the Authority"],
 "Under section 51 an agent who engages a salesperson as an independent contractor is liable for that person's acts and omissions as if the salesperson were an employee."),
("What does a salesperson's licence authorise?",
 "Work on behalf of an agent", ["Work on their own account", "Work for any agent they choose", "Residential rentals only"],
 "A branch manager's or salesperson's licence authorises agency work for or on behalf of an agent (section 49). An agent's licence allows work on the licensee's own account (section 48)."),
("A salesperson moves from one agency to another. What happens to their licence?",
 "It cannot be transferred", ["It passes to the new agent", "It lapses until renewal", "It becomes an agent's licence"],
 "Section 47 says a licence cannot be transferred or vest in anyone other than the person it was granted to. The salesperson remains the licensee and works under the new agent's supervision."),
("An unlicensed person prints \"Property Consultant, Licensed\" on a business card and takes listings. Which offence is clearest?",
 "Holding out as licensed", ["Failing to renew a licence", "Trespass on the property", "Breaching the client's privacy"],
 "Holding out that a person who is neither licensed nor exempt is an agent, branch manager or salesperson is an offence under section 142. Carrying out agency work unlicensed is a separate offence under section 141."),
("An agent keeps paying a salesperson whose licence was cancelled last month. Which offence is the agent committing?",
 "Employing an unlicensed person", ["Failing to display name details", "Misusing a trust account", "Rendering a false account"],
 "Section 143 makes it an offence to employ or continue to employ or contract a person whose licence is suspended or cancelled as an agent, branch manager or salesperson."),
("Which of these is not real estate agency work under the Act?",
 "Lending money on mortgage", ["Marketing a house for a vendor", "Advising on an offer price", "Arranging a commercial lease"],
 "The definition excludes lending money on mortgage or otherwise, investment advice, conveyancing, and publishing or broadcasting advertisements for land or businesses."),
("What makes work \"real estate agency work\" under section 4?",
 "Trade services for another", ["Any property advice given to friends", "Valuing a property for a bank", "Work done by a branch manager"],
 "Agency work means work or services provided in trade, on behalf of another person, for the purpose of bringing about a transaction, including work by a branch manager or salesperson for an agent."),
("A landlord uses a licensee to find a tenant for a residential tenancy covered by the Residential Tenancies Act 1986. Under the Act's definition, that letting is:",
 "Not a transaction", ["A leasehold transaction", "A freehold disposal", "A business sale"],
 "The Act's definition of transaction excludes a tenancy to which the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 applies, so finding a tenant for one is not agency work as defined."),
("When is the sale of shares a transaction for the Act's purposes?",
 "Only if they carry a registrable licence", ["Whenever a company owns some land", "Whenever the shares are worth millions", "Never, shares are always excluded"],
 "Section 4(2) says the sale or purchase of shares is a transaction only if the shares entitle the holder to a licence registrable under the Land Transfer Act 2017."),
("Which past event stops a person being licensed under section 37?",
 "A dishonesty conviction in 10 years", ["Any earlier traffic offence", "An unpaid bank loan of any size", "Working in another industry"],
 "Section 37 bars a person convicted of a crime involving dishonesty within the 10 years before applying. Barred persons also include those prohibited from being company directors."),
("A renewal application has been filed but not decided, and the licence reaches its expiry date. What applies?",
 "It continues until decided", ["It lapses on that day", "It is suspended automatically", "Only current listings may continue"],
 "Section 52(4) says a licence continues in force until a renewal application made before expiry is determined."),
("Before renewing a licence, the Registrar must be satisfied the applicant has:",
 "Done the required education", ["Sold a minimum number of homes", "Employed a part-time assistant", "Paid clients a loyalty bonus"],
 "Section 52(3) adds to the usual checks that the applicant has completed any continuing education required by practice rules made under section 15."),
("Which body maintains the register of licensees through its Registrar?",
 "The Real Estate Authority", ["The Law Society of NZ", "The Commerce Commission", "The Institute of REINZ"],
 "The Authority (operating as REA) appoints a Registrar and ensures the register of licensees is established and kept (section 12). It also receives complaints about licensees."),
("A salesperson sells land by auction on behalf of their agent. Must the salesperson also be a registered auctioneer?",
 "No, the licence is an exemption", ["Yes, in every single case", "Yes, but only for rural land", "Yes, after the first year"],
 "A branch manager's or salesperson's licence authorises selling land by auction on behalf of the agent and operates as an exemption from registering under the Auctioneers Act 2013 (section 49)."),
]
